{
 "gdd": "command-simulation-layer",
 "blocking": [
  "[RECOMMENDED] States and Transitions L180-198 / CR-18 / KRN-STATE-01, KRN-STATE-02: [main review, confirmed by creative-director] Row L181 'BOOTING | Registries valid and frozen -> LOADING' carries no seed or payload, and no row covers (BOOTING, request_new_game) or (BOOTING, request_restore). L191 lists request_new_game only from RUNNING/PAUSED/FAULTED. Under L198 ('every other pair is invalid') the first-boot new game that KRN-STATE-02 relies on is an invalid transition. The intent can be read from L181's note, so this is not a blocker, but it is the top fix: it is the very first path the game takes. Requests queued during SAVING/LOADING also have no named DEFERRED outcome.",
  "[RECOMMENDED] CR-15 / KRN-EPO-05 / OQ 24: [main review] The kernel asserts SL_RESTORE_EPOCH_NOT_DURABLE. The publisher (Save/Load) and the registry spell it SL_EPOCH_NOT_DURABLE, and under G1 the publisher's spelling wins. KRN-EPO-05 would therefore fail against the real Save/Load.",
  "[RECOMMENDED] Cross-GDD: web-map-and-transit.md / registry web_commands vs CR-6: [main review, confirmed by creative-director] web-map-and-transit.md has no actor_binding or actor_source declaration for the PLAYER commands pod_hop, berth and unberth. Its only hit is L1427, which is about the SYSTEM rows. No other GDD declares them either: a repo-wide grep for pod_hop near actor_binding/OWNED_BY_ISSUER/actor_source returned nothing. Registry L1307 lists player_origin with no binding. Under CR-6 ('no silent default') the composition root would fault at boot. The defect is in the sibling GDD; the kernel contract itself is unambiguous, so it does not block this document."
 ]
}
